---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Getting Started">
  <h1 style="font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Getting Started</h1>
  <p style="color: #6b7280; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Install Cognivo and start building AI-powered interfaces in minutes.</p>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Installation</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Install the core package and an adapter for your AI provider:</p>
    <pre><code>pnpm add @cognivo/core @cognivo/adapter-openai</code></pre>
    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">For UI components and design tokens (Lit web components):</p>
    <pre><code>pnpm add @cognivo/components @cognivo/tokens</code></pre>
    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">For the cognitive bias design advisor:</p>
    <pre><code>pnpm add @cognivo/design-advisor</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Quick Start: AI Client</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Create an AI client with the OpenAI adapter and send your first request:</p>
    <pre><code>import {'{'} ContextBuilder, AiIntent {'}'} from '@cognivo/core';
import {'{'} OpenAiClient {'}'} from '@cognivo/adapter-openai';

// 1. Create a client
const client = new OpenAiClient({'{'} apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY {'}'});

// 2. Build context with your data
const context = new ContextBuilder()
  .withDataset([{'{'} revenue: 50000, month: 'Jan' {'}'}, {'{'} revenue: 62000, month: 'Feb' {'}'}])
  .withIntent(AiIntent.Summarize)
  .build();

// 3. Send the request
const result = await client.run(context);</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Quick Start: Components</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Import the components package to register all custom elements, then use them in your HTML:</p>
    <pre><code>import '@cognivo/components';

// Now use in HTML:
// &lt;ai-thinking text="Analyzing..."&gt;&lt;/ai-thinking&gt;
// &lt;ai-badge score="0.92"&gt;&lt;/ai-badge&gt;
// &lt;ai-chat&gt;&lt;/ai-chat&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Quick Start: Generative UI</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Stream AI-generated UI components in real time with the gen-ui packages:</p>
    <pre><code>pnpm add @cognivo/gen-ui @cognivo/gen-ui-lit</code></pre>
    <pre style="margin-top: 1rem;"><code>import {'{'} cognivoLibrary, createStreamingParser {'}'} from '@cognivo/gen-ui';
import {'{'} LitRenderer {'}'} from '@cognivo/gen-ui-lit';

const renderer = new LitRenderer(cognivoLibrary);
const parser = createStreamingParser(cognivoLibrary.toJSONSchema());

for await (const token of llmStream) {'{'}
  const result = parser.push(token);
  if (result.root) renderer.render(result, container);
{'}'}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Quick Start: Design Advisor</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Access the cognitive bias library to improve your design decisions:</p>
    <pre><code>import {'{'} BiasRegistry, queryBiases {'}'} from '@cognivo/design-advisor';

// Search for biases relevant to pricing pages
const biases = queryBiases({'{'} tags: ['pricing', 'conversion'] {'}'});

// Get a specific bias
import {'{'} anchoringBias {'}'} from '@cognivo/design-advisor';
console.log(anchoringBias.name);        // "Anchoring Bias"
console.log(anchoringBias.description); // Full description with design implications</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Dark Mode</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">All components and tokens support dark mode out of the box. Set the <code>data-theme</code> attribute on your root element:</p>
    <pre><code>&lt;html data-theme="dark"&gt;</code></pre>
    <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #6b7280;">All <code>--cg-*</code> tokens automatically adapt to the selected theme.</p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Interactive Showcase</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">See all 125 components in action with live examples:</p>
    <p><a href="/showcase.html" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; background: var(--color-primary); color: white; padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; text-decoration: none;">View Showcase &rarr;</a></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Next Steps</h2>
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;">
      <a href="/components" style="display: block; background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
        <strong style="display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Components</strong>
        <span style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 0.9rem;">Explore 125 web components</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/core" style="display: block; background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
        <strong style="display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Core API</strong>
        <span style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 0.9rem;">AiClient, intents, context building</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/patterns" style="display: block; background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
        <strong style="display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">AI Patterns</strong>
        <span style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 0.9rem;">12 production-ready integration patterns</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
